1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:03,564
Some people would rather talk than type.

2
00:00:03,564 --> 00:00:08,022
This video shows how to set up a spoken conversation with an AI assistant:

3
00:00:08,022 --> 00:00:13,205
the speech deployments, the cascaded realtime deployment that chains them, and the chat

4
00:00:13,205 --> 00:00:15,880
mode that puts a voice button in the chat.

5
00:00:20,480 --> 00:00:23,928
A spoken conversation needs a realtime deployment.

6
00:00:23,928 --> 00:00:28,669
Some providers offer a model that listens and speaks by itself, and you

7
00:00:28,669 --> 00:00:30,270
can use it directly.

8
00:00:31,020 --> 00:00:36,431
When none of your providers does, a cascaded realtime deployment chains three deployments

9
00:00:36,431 --> 00:00:38,026
that you already have:

10
00:00:38,026 --> 00:00:43,380
one that transcribes speech, a chat model that writes the reply, and one that speaks it.

11
00:00:44,130 --> 00:00:47,882
Either way, the profile and the chat look the same.

12
00:00:47,882 --> 00:00:53,676
Tools, data sources and instructions keep working, and typed and spoken turns land

13
00:00:53,676 --> 00:00:55,190
in the same chat.

14
00:00:59,490 --> 00:01:02,640
The cascade starts with speech deployments.

15
00:01:02,640 --> 00:01:09,455
Open Artificial Intelligence, Deployments, click Add Deployment, and click Add on Azure AI Services.

16
00:01:09,455 --> 00:01:12,670
This is the provider of the speech services.

17
00:01:13,137 --> 00:01:17,617
Enter the Model name and a Technical name, then the Endpoint of the

18
00:01:17,617 --> 00:01:20,317
speech service and its Authentication.

19
00:01:20,317 --> 00:01:23,937
The API key is stored securely and never shown again.

20
00:01:24,450 --> 00:01:31,107
On the Model capabilities card, tick Speech to text, and Realtime, for a deployment that transcribes.

21
00:01:31,107 --> 00:01:35,151
A deployment that speaks has Text to speech ticked instead.

22
00:01:35,151 --> 00:01:36,520
Then click Save.

23
00:01:40,782 --> 00:01:45,849
Now click Add Deployment again, and click Add on Cascaded Realtime.

24
00:01:45,849 --> 00:01:49,042
Enter a Model name and a Technical name.

25
00:01:49,525 --> 00:01:52,071
Choose the three deployments it chains:

26
00:01:52,071 --> 00:01:57,048
the one that transcribes speech, the chat deployment that generates the reply, and

27
00:01:57,048 --> 00:01:58,689
the one that speaks it.

28
00:01:58,689 --> 00:02:02,195
Each list offers only the deployments that fit its role.

29
00:02:02,664 --> 00:02:09,199
A cascade is realtime by construction, so the deployment declares the Realtime feature for you.

30
00:02:09,199 --> 00:02:10,298
Click Save.

31
00:02:10,298 --> 00:02:14,374
It now appears wherever a realtime deployment is offered.

32
00:02:18,595 --> 00:02:21,290
Open Settings, Artificial Intelligence.

33
00:02:21,290 --> 00:02:27,758
Default speech-to-text deployment and Default text-to-speech deployment are used by features that only

34
00:02:27,758 --> 00:02:29,615
transcribe or only speak.

35
00:02:30,159 --> 00:02:35,518
Default realtime deployment is the model of a spoken conversation, when a profile

36
00:02:35,518 --> 00:02:37,243
does not name its own.

37
00:02:37,243 --> 00:02:41,679
Leave it empty, and the first realtime-capable deployment is used.

38
00:02:45,902 --> 00:02:47,485
Open the profile.

39
00:02:47,485 --> 00:02:51,338
On the Content tab, set Chat mode to Conversation.

40
00:02:51,338 --> 00:02:56,292
Text only is typing, and Audio input adds a microphone to dictate.

41
00:02:56,799 --> 00:03:02,931
Choose the Conversation deployment, the realtime deployment that carries the spoken conversation.

42
00:03:02,931 --> 00:03:05,609
Leave it empty to use the site default.

43
00:03:06,147 --> 00:03:09,278
Choose the Voice that the assistant speaks with.

44
00:03:09,278 --> 00:03:12,408
The voices come from the deployment that speaks.

45
00:03:12,408 --> 00:03:16,872
Enable text-to-speech playback adds a read aloud button to the answers.

46
00:03:16,872 --> 00:03:17,857
Click Save.

47
00:03:22,116 --> 00:03:24,039
Open a chat with the profile.

48
00:03:24,039 --> 00:03:28,544
Beside the message box there is now a sound-wave button, Start speaking, and

49
00:03:28,544 --> 00:03:31,236
the message box is still there, for typing.

50
00:03:31,735 --> 00:03:35,595
Click it and allow the microphone, and the session starts.

51
00:03:35,595 --> 00:03:38,732
The message box gives way to End Conversation.

52
00:03:38,732 --> 00:03:41,808
Speak, and your sentences appear in the chat.

53
00:03:41,808 --> 00:03:45,005
To interrupt the assistant, just start talking.

54
00:03:45,489 --> 00:03:47,668
Click End Conversation to stop.

55
00:03:47,668 --> 00:03:52,145
The message box comes back, and what you type continues the same chat.

56
00:03:52,145 --> 00:03:57,269
Here we only show where the button is, because a conversation needs a microphone.

57
00:04:01,469 --> 00:04:06,509
Use headphones, so that the assistant does not hear its own voice through your speakers.

58
00:04:07,259 --> 00:04:11,938
A cascade adds some delay before the assistant starts to speak, because a

59
00:04:11,938 --> 00:04:14,366
turn passes through three services.

60
00:04:14,366 --> 00:04:17,149
A model that speaks by itself is quicker.

61
00:04:17,899 --> 00:04:22,179
On a live voice model, a gear lets each person pick the microphone

62
00:04:22,179 --> 00:04:26,281
and speaker, and turn push-to-talk and interruptions on or off.

63
00:04:26,281 --> 00:04:28,599
These are saved in their browser.

64
00:04:30,599 --> 00:04:35,707
Add the speech deployments, chain them in a cascaded realtime deployment, and set

65
00:04:35,707 --> 00:04:37,586
a profile to Conversation.

66
00:04:37,586 --> 00:04:39,583
Your assistant can now talk.

67
00:04:39,583 --> 00:04:41,109
Thanks for watching.

